    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present to the market this beautifully refurbished and exceptionally charming detached bungalow at 27 Shanid Road, a wonderful property ideally positioned within this quiet and highly sought-after enclave in the heart of Harold's Cross. Renovated approximately seven years ago and further enhanced with a stylish kitchen upgrade in 2020, this bright and spacious residence combines modern comfort with an unrivalled location. Tucked away just off Clareville Road, Shanid Road enjoys a peaceful residential atmosphere that offers an almost country-like sense of tranquillity, despite being just minutes from the city centre and an array of superb local amenities. No. 27 represents a rare opportunity to acquire a truly unique home on generous gardens, offering excellent potential for future extension or reconfiguration, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe accommodation is both modern and highly functional, extending to well-proportioned living spaces designed to maximise natural light throughout. Upon entering, a welcoming entrance hallway leads to a large open-plan living and dining room positioned to the front of the property, creating a superb space for both everyday living and entertaining. The contemporary kitchen was upgraded in 2020 and there are two spacious double bedrooms and a well-appointed family bathroom. Outside, the home is complemented by sunny rear and side gardens with desirable southerly aspects, providing wonderful outdoor space for relaxing, entertaining or further development potential. \n\nShanid Road is a quiet cul-de-sac tucked away off Clareville Road, offering residents a unique sense of privacy and tranquillity within easy reach of a wealth of local amenities. Harold's Cross, Terenure and Rathmines are all nearby, providing an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, shops and recreational facilities. The city centre is easily accessible by foot, bicycle or the many regular bus routes servicing the area, making this an ideal location for commuters and families alike. The property is also within close proximity to a range of highly regarded primary and secondary schools, parks and sporting facilities, further enhancing the appeal of this superb residential address. This is a rare opportunity to acquire a turnkey home in one of Dublin's most convenient and established residential locations, and viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this exceptional property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.96m x 1.44m\n\n\nLiving/Dining Room - 5.25m x 4.44m\n\n\nKitchen - 3.65m x 2.61m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.74m x 2.91m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.65m x 3.11m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.25m x 1.64m\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Recently renovated 1970's detached bungalow</li><li> Set on a cul-de-sac, with quiet surroundings</li><li> Superb potential to extend if one desires</li><li> New kitchen installed in 2020</li><li> GFCH - with recent gas boiler</li><li> Sunny rear and side gardens, with Southerly aspects</li><li> Convenient location within a stone's throw of Harold's Cross, Terenure, Rathgar and Rathmines villages</li><li> Close to every possible amenity to include excellent shops, cafes, restaurants, parks and recreation</li><li> Easy access to city centre</li><li> Close to a selection of nearby bus routes to the city centre and beyond</li><li> The M50 road network is also easily accessible, connecting to all major national routes.</ul>"
      },
